1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,287
The library is words — trillions of pieces of text, like the ones you type.

2
00:00:05,287 --> 00:00:10,823
The reading room is chips, thousands of them, running day and night for months.

3
00:00:10,823 --> 00:00:11,929
And the teachers?

4
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:13,115
They're engineers.

5
00:00:13,115 --> 00:00:14,745
India has the teachers.

6
00:00:14,745 --> 00:00:16,023
You know this already.

7
00:00:16,023 --> 00:00:19,738
Indian engineers write software for companies all over the world.

8
00:00:19,738 --> 00:00:23,002
So our missing pieces are the library and the reading room.

9
00:00:23,002 --> 00:00:24,640
Let's start with the library.

10
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,108
Almost nobody tells you about this part.

11
00:00:27,108 --> 00:00:29,841
A lot of A.I. learns from the internet.

12
00:00:29,841 --> 00:00:33,757
One of the biggest free copies of the web is called Common Crawl.

13
00:00:33,757 --> 00:00:39,950
Many A.I. models learned from it, including an early model from the makers of the Chat G.P.T. you use.

14
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:48,564
So we took its latest copy, from October twenty twenty-six — more than two billion web pages — and checked its own count of languages.

15
00:00:48,564 --> 00:00:49,390
English?

16
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:52,100
Forty-two out of every hundred pages.

17
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,783
Now, can you guess Hindi?

18
00:00:53,783 --> 00:00:58,545
For every one page in Hindi... there are about two hundred pages in English.

19
00:00:58,545 --> 00:01:02,190
And Hindi is the mother tongue of more than fifty crore people.

20
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:02,973
Marathi?

21
00:01:02,973 --> 00:01:04,383
About fifteen hundred.

22
00:01:04,383 --> 00:01:05,096
Telugu?

23
00:01:05,096 --> 00:01:06,993
About two thousand three hundred.

24
00:01:06,993 --> 00:01:11,763
And each of those is the mother tongue of around eight crore people, maybe yours.

25
00:01:11,763 --> 00:01:16,903
All of India's languages together make up less than one page in every hundred.

26
00:01:16,903 --> 00:01:17,791
Think about it.

27
00:01:17,791 --> 00:01:22,159
More than one in every six people on Earth lives in our country.

28
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:26,960
But in the library these machines read, our language is almost invisible.

